<Window
    x:Class="TransPeek.Views.RegionSelectWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- RootGrid is focusable (IsTabStop) so keyboard input reaches this
         window: v0.1 relied only on a KeyboardAccelerator, but a plain
         Grid never takes keyboard focus, so Esc did nothing and the user
         was trapped fullscreen with no button to click. There are now
         three independent ways out: Esc, right-click, and Alt+F4
         (window Closed completes the selection task). The Cancel button
         was removed (2026-11-14, 0.1.3.59 test): it sat top-right near
         the mouse and an accidental click on it exited the capture; Esc
         on the keyboard, right-click and Alt+F4 already cover the exit,
         and the grid keeps keyboard focus so Esc is reliable.
         NO dim layer (removed 2026-11-13, Manh): the 15% dim was
         suspected of filling color instead of dimming (the user picks
         blind when the overlay renders opaque); no dim is needed to
         signal capture mode — the cursor changes to the capture shape
         while dragging. The selection rectangle keeps its light fill
         (#22FFFFFF) so the picked region stays visible. NO hint chip
         (removed 2026-11-14, 0.1.3.65 test): the floating "Esc" chip sat
         top-center where the mouse works, and hovering it exited the
         capture — Esc on the keyboard, right-click and Alt+F4 already
         cover the exit, and Manh knows them.
         BackgroundImage (0.1.3.54): the window renders opaque, so the
         dim alone shows only a flat grey board — the user picks blind
         and a capture taken while the overlay is up photographs the
         overlay, not the desktop. The display screenshot (captured
         before the overlay appears) is the background instead, so the
         user sees the real desktop, and the region is cropped
         out of that same screenshot. -->
    <Grid x:Name="RootGrid" IsTabStop="True">
        <Image x:Name="BackgroundImage" Stretch="Fill" />
        <Canvas x:Name="SelectionCanvas">
            <Rectangle x:Name="SelectionRect" Stroke="White" StrokeThickness="2"
                       Fill="#22FFFFFF" Visibility="Collapsed" />
        </Canvas>
    </Grid>
</Window>
